WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.300
In under two minutes, you will add an event to the map.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.336
We start on the map.

00:00:05.235 --> 00:00:08.567
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.975
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:15.464
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:15.464 --> 00:00:16.810
Tap Use my location.

00:00:18.554 --> 00:00:20.770
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:21.422
Tap Allow.

00:00:24.999 --> 00:00:27.495
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:28.713
See the three dots?

00:00:28.713 --> 00:00:29.260
Tap them.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.443
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:34.209 --> 00:00:35.149
Tap An event.

00:00:37.214 --> 00:00:40.214
If your event has a web page, paste it here.

00:00:40.214 --> 00:00:41.614
If not, tap No, Next.

00:00:43.393 --> 00:00:46.681
Type the event's name, and choose a season and type.

00:00:46.681 --> 00:00:47.549
Then tap Next.

00:00:51.441 --> 00:00:53.461
Pick the first and last day.

00:00:53.461 --> 00:00:54.436
Then tap Next.

00:00:56.929 --> 00:00:58.048
Free or paid?

00:00:58.048 --> 00:00:59.646
Tap Free, then Next.

00:01:02.189 --> 00:01:05.309
Type the place, the city, and the street address.

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:06.183
Then tap Next.

00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:12.595
Describe it in a sentence or two.

00:01:12.595 --> 00:01:13.533
Then tap Next.

00:01:17.894 --> 00:01:20.437
Check everything, and tap Add my event.

00:01:22.462 --> 00:01:24.843
Next up: Show off your house.
